@HD	VN:1.6	SO:unsorted	GO:query
@SQ	SN:chr1	LN:240
@SQ	SN:chr2	LN:240
@CO	09-edge-cases-and-mate-fields: one template for each case drawn in the reference section "Edge cases and how they are resolved". Copied from examples 01, 03 and 05.
@CO	(a) pair_overlap: 60 bp fragment chr1:41-100, reads 40/40, 20-base overlap chr1:61-80.
@CO	(b) hic_sup_overlap: molecule chr1:41-100(+) | chr2:101-140(+), L=100, bisulfite-converted. R1 (80 bp) = primary 60M20S chr1:41 + supplementary 60H20M chr2:101 (MAPQ 40). R2 (35 bp) = 35M chr2:106 (-). R2 overlaps only the supplementary.
@CO	(c) primary_inside_overlap: molecule chr2:141-160(+) | chr1:41-120(+), L=100, reads 80/80. R1 primary 20S60M chr1:41 (MAPQ 20) lies wholly inside the overlap; its supplementary 20M60H chr2:141 (MAPQ 60) does not.
@CO	(d) read_through: dovetailing mates. 30 bp molecule chr1:161-190 read with 40 bp reads; each read ends in 10 soft-clipped adapter bases that reach past the other read's 5' end.
